  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid and HUVEC, mediated through dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Javanicoside F and Astersaponin F, both of which are known to interact with HUVEC cells. The shared target of these compounds implies a potential mechanism by which 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid influences HUVEC function. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, reinforcing the notion that the compound may act through a common biological mechanism involving protein kinases. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid exerts its effects on HUVEC via a pathway that involves protein kinase activity, potentially modulating cellular processes in these cells.",
